{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3565","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3565","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3565\",\"parent_revision\":\"ecbcf0b690aac06f80e671a43f3d830db9e5a59f937d72f66c38f34a5b8fe1e8\",\"root_revision\":\"ecbcf0b690aac06f80e671a43f3d830db9e5a59f937d72f66c38f34a5b8fe1e8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_list(status=...)` compares the requested value with each item's derived status by exact string match (`backlog_core/operations.py` `_filter_open_items`, via `_item_derived_status`). Each backend reports \\\"in progress\\\" as a different value, or not at all, so no single status value finds in-progress items on every backend.\\n\\n| Backend | How \\\"in progress\\\" is written | Value the status filter compares | Matches `in-progress` |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| GitHub | issue label `status:in-progress` (`gh_client.apply_status_in_progress`) | the `status:`-prefixed label (`gh_client.py` batch status fetch) | no; needs `status:in-progress` |\\n| Beads | native status column via `bd update --claim` (`beads_backend.py` `apply_status_in_progress`) | native `in_progress` (`beads_backend.py` `list_work_items`; `test_beads_backend.py` asserts `item.status == \\\"in_progress\\\"`) | no; needs `in_progress` |\\n| SQLite | a tag, `_tag_issue(item, \\\"in-progress\\\")`; the `status` column stays `open` | the `status` column (`sqlite_backend.py` `batch_fetch_statuses`) | never |\\n| Memory | no-op (`memory_backend.py` `apply_status_in_progress`) | issue state lowercased, `open`/`closed` | never |\\n\\nThe `backlog_list` MCP parameter documents `'status:in-progress'` as its example value, and `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` filters with `status=\\\"status:in-progress\\\"`, so the GitHub spelling is the only one exercised.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA skill cannot ask \\\"which items are in progress?\\\" in a backend-neutral way. `work-backlog-item`'s quick workflow asked it with `status=\\\"in-progress\\\"`, which matched nothing on any backend; #3427 removes that integration step rather than encode one backend's spelling.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: fix work on #3427, 2026-09-15\\n- **Research**: beads status is a native column with built-in values including `in_progress`; beads labels are free-form strings unrelated to status (`docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/02-beads-data-model.md` \u00a72 and \u00a76).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Proposed Direction\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nMap each backend's native value to one logical status inside backlog_core before filtering, so `status=\\\"in-progress\\\"` matches a GitHub `status:in-progress` label, a beads `in_progress` issue and an SQLite in-progress tag. Each backend needs a red test showing an in-progress item the filter currently misses.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e507654e9637f81053cca52f9458a216dd139276114af5684631e0736c223f89\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUeS-Iw\"}"}